NPC dialog portraits
--------------------

Source: "500 Fantasy Pixel Art Portraits" by Batareya (batareya.itch.io,
https://batareya.itch.io/500-fantasy-pixel-art-portraits-a-world-of-characters-for-your-projects).
License: 100 percent free for personal and commercial use, attribution not
required. The portraits were produced with AI assistance by the author. The
full terms are in content/portraits/LICENSE.txt. Attribution is given here
because the author appreciates it.

Thirty portraits from the pack were scaled to the game's 64x64 format: six
for the interactible NPCs, and a pool of twenty-four that a player-character
cycles through at creation.

Spell icons
-----------

Source: "MAGE ICONS BIG PACK" by Batareya (batareya.itch.io). The art is 64x64
pixel icons distributed at 8x upscale. The icons under content/icons are the
subset that content/spells.txt names, scaled back to their native 64x64.
License: Batareya's asset packs are offered for free personal and commercial
use; confirm the exact terms for this pack against its itch.io page before a
release. See content/icons/LICENSE.txt for the spell-to-icon mapping.

Spell catalog
-------------

Source: the AX&X spell lists (the author's own two-page OSR ruleset, a refit
of the classic 1st Edition advanced rules). content/spells.txt is imported
from that project's spells.csv: the Cleric, Druid, and Magic-User lists across
six spell levels, with each spell's terse effect prose kept as the behaviour.
The spell names follow the long-standing lineage AX&X refits.

The crawler reads the prose as the real behaviour and maps each spell's damage
type onto its own five elements thematically, so combat that wires a spell up
approximates the intent rather than reproducing exact tabletop mechanics.
